        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Grigory Margulis, Leonid Levin\n- Roles: mathematician, computer scientist\n- Concepts: lattices in Lie groups, ergodic theory, diophantine approximation, differential geometry, Margulis lemma, discrete subgroups, isometries, non-positively curved Riemannian manifolds, hyperbolic n-space\n\nFacts:\n- Grigory Margulis was born on February 24, 1946.\n- Leonid Levin was born on November 2, 1948.\n- Grigory Margulis is a Russian-American mathematician.\n- Grigory Margulis is known for his work on lattices in Lie groups.\n- Grigory Margulis introduced methods from ergodic theory into diophantine approximation.\n- Leonid Levin is a Soviet-American computer scientist.\n- The Margulis lemma is named after Grigory Margulis.\n- The Margulis lemma is a result in differential geometry.\n- The Margulis lemma concerns discrete subgroups of isometries of non-positively curved Riemannian manifolds such as hyperbolic n-space.",
